          "text_matches": [
            {
              "property": "content",
              "fragment": "| A328611 | 11, October 31, 2019 | `273ca073f7b24d3ff7ccb59d92f72e14ba0ce7ea` |\n| A327315 | 6, November 6, 2019 | `47efe5bcf666241a43536ea4f106e7342c741f96` |\n",
              "matches": [
                {
                  "text": "A327315",
                  "indices": [
                    82,
                    89
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "property": "content",
              "fragment": "\nA327315 is a different rational function and a different irreducibility classification. Its conjecture is not covered by the odd-degree theorem under audit. The companion references A094440 and A094441 were read in full: they give related Fibonacci/binomial row polynomials, known formulas, and different derivative numerators. Neither checked record contains a proof of the A326925 irreducibility assertion.\n",
              "matches": [
                {
                  "text": "A327315",
                  "indices": [
                    1,
                    8
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/blakestone-x/math/blob/2422f82913949a4f4a4db7c7616b09c43546aea7/A326925/AUDIT.md",
          "path": "A326925/AUDIT.md",
          "display_url": "https://github.com/blakestone-x/math/blob/2422f82913949a4f4a4db7c7616b09c43546aea7/A326925/AUDIT.md",
          "display_title": "A326925/AUDIT.md",
          "text_matches": [
            {
              "property": "content",
              "fragment": "\nThe result concerns one recorded clause: every odd-degree polynomial in this family is irreducible. It also proves irreducibility over the larger quadratic field, the exact degree, and the correspondence with reduced derivative numerators. These stronger statements and supporting lemmas are consequences and proof components, not additional conjecture resolutions. The even-degree factorization clause and A327315 are explicitly outside the claimed result.\n",
              "matches": [
                {
                  "text": "A327315",
                  "indices": [
                    408,
                    415
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "property": "content",
              "fragment": "\nThe related A328610 and A328611 exports describe the separate even-degree factors, while A327315 uses a different rational function. None is silently substituted for the family proved here. The four preserved source files were checked against their recorded Git blob hashes.\n",
              "matches": [
                {
                  "text": "A327315",
                  "indices": [
                    90,
                    97
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/blakestone-x/math/blob/2422f82913949a4f4a4db7c7616b09c43546aea7/A326925/audit-verification.txt",
