        {
          "url": "https://github.com/blakestone-x/math/blob/2422f82913949a4f4a4db7c7616b09c43546aea7/A326925/README.md",
          "path": "A326925/README.md",
          "display_url": "https://github.com/blakestone-x/math/blob/2422f82913949a4f4a4db7c7616b09c43546aea7/A326925/README.md",
          "display_title": "A326925/README.md",
          "text_matches": [
            {
              "property": "content",
              "fragment": "Some auxiliary golden-ratio nonpower lemmas are included, but they are not counted as additional conjecture resolutions and do not establish the even-degree clause.\n\n## Sources and historical scope\n\nThe conjecture is attributed in A326925 to Clark Kimberling in 2019. The exact primary export and three related entries are preserved in `sources/`. Both search engines, the current trureturing index, and nearby Fibonacci-polynomial literature were checked. No earlier proof of this exact odd-degree assertion was located. This is a bounded prior-publication search, not a certification of historical priority; details and exact source hashes are in [source_checks.md](source_checks.md).\n\nThe complete independent audit and build logs are included with the package. The source-index discrepancy is documented rather than counted as another resolution, and no result for A327315 or the separate even-degree family is claimed.",
              "matches": [
                {
